    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0591" n="579" xml:id="pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/2–446: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Schoenrich</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-02-05T18:00:00-05:00">February 5, 1946—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Immediately following telegram contains text of a message received from
                    Anglo-American Committee of Enquiry, now in London, for communication to Govts
                    of Iraq, Egypt, Saudi Arabia, Syria and Lebanon.</p>
                <p>Officers in charge missions in foregoing countries should join their respective
                    British colleagues in presenting this communication to the Govts to which they
                    are accredited. British Foreign Office has already forwarded message to its
                    representatives in foregoing countries with similar instructions. In presenting
                    communication it should be made clear that you are forwarding a message from
                    Committee only and that Committee’s consideration of views of Arab states does
                    not constitute the consultations to which this Govt is committed in advance of
                    any basic change of policy in Palestine.</p>
                <p>Consular officers in charge at Jerusalem and Aden should similarly communicate
                    the Committee’s message to Govts of Trans-Jordan and Yemen, where British
                    Colonial Office is taking parallel action.</p>
                <p>Sent to Baghdad, repeated to Cairo, Jidda, Jerusalem, Aden and Beirut (for
                    repetition to Damascus). Also repeated to London for Judge Hutcheson.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
